{
  "rules": [
    "When sentiment is near zero (0.00) and recent history shows a downtrend or consolidation, the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate volatility.",
    "The model exhibits a significant lag in recognizing sudden price spikes; forecasts remain flat while true outcomes surge sharply after 10-15 days.",
    "Apply a downward correction to the forecast when the last 3 days of history are below the 7-day moving average, even if sentiment is neutral.",
    "Reduce forecast confidence by 15-20% during periods where sentiment history shows no positive momentum despite rising historical prices.",
    "Expect mean reversion errors: the model tends to project linear growth when true outcomes oscillate within a narrow band before a breakout."
  ]
}
